{%- comment -%}
  Shopify's own robots rules are emitted verbatim via robots.default_groups —
  they already block /checkout, /cart, /account, /orders and the sort_by
  permutations, and they already advertise the sitemap. Hand-rolling a
  replacement is how stores accidentally deindex themselves, so this template
  only appends.

  Whitespace control matters more than usual here: robots.txt is line-oriented,
  and a stripped newline silently fuses "User-agent: *" onto the first Disallow,
  which voids the whole group. Every newline below is deliberate.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
{{ group.user_agent }}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{{ rule }}
{% endfor %}{% if group.sitemap != blank %}{{ group.sitemap }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
# --- Apex additions ---
# Faceted and preview URLs only. Everything else is already covered by the
# default groups above, and the sitemap is already advertised there — repeating
# it here just produced four identical Sitemap lines.
User-agent: *
Disallow: /*?*filter.*
Disallow: /*preview_theme_id*
Disallow: /*preview_script_id*

# --- AI and answer-engine crawlers ---
# These agents are already permitted by the "User-agent: *" group above, so the
# groups below do not unlock anything new. They are here because several of
# these crawlers are operated by companies that treat an explicit, named group
# as the publisher's stated position, and because a named group is the only
# place a per-agent Crawl-delay or future carve-out can live. Making the stance
# explicit also means a later "block everything unfamiliar" edit by an app or a
# consultant cannot quietly take Apex out of AI answers.
#
# Two rules matter when reading this:
#   1. A crawler obeys exactly one group — the most specific one naming it. So
#      each group below has to repeat the checkout, account and cart exclusions;
#      they are NOT inherited from "User-agent: *". Deleting a Disallow line
#      here opens that path to that crawler.
#   2. Google-Extended controls Gemini and AI Overview *training* only and has
#      no effect on Google Search ranking. Disallowing it removes Apex from AI
#      answers without winning anything back, which is why it is allowed here.
{% assign ai_agents = 'GPTBot,OAI-SearchBot,ChatGPT-User,ClaudeBot,Claude-User,Claude-SearchBot,anthropic-ai,PerplexityBot,Perplexity-User,Google-Extended,Applebot-Extended,Amazonbot,Meta-ExternalAgent,Meta-ExternalFetcher,DuckAssistBot,YouBot,cohere-ai,Bytespider,MistralAI-User,Diffbot,Timpibot' | split: ',' %}
{% for agent in ai_agents %}User-agent: {{ agent }}
{% endfor %}Allow: /
Disallow: /admin
Disallow: /cart
Disallow: /carts
Disallow: /checkout
Disallow: /checkouts/
Disallow: /orders
Disallow: /account
Disallow: /search
Disallow: /*?*filter.*
Disallow: /*preview_theme_id*
Disallow: /*preview_script_id*
Disallow: /*?*oseid=*
